  "definition": "Fear of strangers is an intense or irrational fear or dislike of people seen as strange, unfamiliar, or foreign. It can also describe a hostile attitude toward perceived outsiders that shows up in prejudice, rejection, exclusion, or vilifying of non-natives.",
